{
  "run_id": "PMC11433250__broad__pcd_PCD_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Conventional Fe–B or other boride-based steel components are used in hot-dip aluminum-plating equipment.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pack aluminizing at approximately 800°C for 2–4 hours in an inert or slightly reducing atmosphere will deposit an aluminide layer on the boride-based substrate.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed pack-aluminized layer can be kept below 10 μm in thickness.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled cooling after aluminizing will maintain a uniform, thin diffusion layer.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An inert or slightly reducing atmosphere will prevent unwanted oxidation during pack aluminizing.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will create a continuous, adherent, dense aluminide layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Upon exposure to molten aluminum, the aluminide layer will oxidize rapidly to form a stable Al2O3 scale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::017::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alumina can form a compact diffusion barrier that hinders further transport or oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::017::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina scale will be self-healing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina scale will be chemically inert in molten aluminum.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The aluminide/alumina barrier will limit molten-aluminum infiltration into the boride substrate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::017::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC6908586::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting aluminum infiltration will mitigate corrosion of the underlying boride substrate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pack-aluminized boride-based components will have lower molten-aluminum penetration and corrosion rates than untreated components.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reduction in molten-aluminum penetration or corrosion rate may be approximately 40–50%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protection will remain effective at typical hot-dip aluminum-plating temperatures and exposure durations if the aluminide thickness remains controlled.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlling the aluminide-layer thickness will avoid compromising mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
